It was as if he had given milk to a venomous snake. For the sake of examining that, Shambhurmurdhi Kilasurah. He who is self-created, is not created by the self. 23 ज़a. Meaning of the word

Sah—He; Tat—His (of Shiva); Var—Of the boon; Pariksha-Artham—To take the test; Shambhohi—Of Shivji; Murdhn—On the head; Kil—Undoubtedly; Asurah—The Asuras; Swah—Own; Hastam—Hand; Dhatum—To keep; Aarebhe—Tried; Sahah—He; Abibhyat—Got scared; Swah—By oneself; Krutat—From doing; Shivah—Shiva..

To test the boon of Lord Shambhu, the Asura tried to put his hand on his head.

Tried. Then Shiva began to fear what he had done. Tenopasthah sannastah paradhavansapethuthu.
Yavadantam divo bhumih kashtanaam udagadu udakam. 2. Meaning of the word

Ten—by him; Upasrishta—being chased; Sannrasta—frightened; Paradhavan—running; Sa—with; Vepathu— trembling;
Yavat—up to; Antam— end; Divah— of the sky; Bhumih— of the earth; Kashtanaam— of the directions; Udagat— quickly;
Gaya; Udak— from the north direction. When the demon started chasing him, Shivji, trembling with fear, started running quickly from his residence located in the north. As far as the earth, sky, and the ends of the universe are, they
remained as servants. Ajanantah pratividhim tushnimasurasheshwaraah. Then, the one who departed from Vaikuntha, the radiant one, the supreme darkness. 25. Yatra Narayana saaksha nyasinaam paramo gatiha.
Of the minds, of the erected heads, where the one who has gone returns. 26. Meaning of the word

